<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70989" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νομοθετ-έω</span></b> , pf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νενομοθέτηκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					126.13
				</span></i>
			:—<i>frame laws,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				15.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				534d
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λακεδαιμονίοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					15
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς μοναρχίαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					2.8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					11.40
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1294a37
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὲρ ὅλου τοῦ ἐμπορίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					56.48
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i>frame laws for oneself,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				398b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tht.</u>
				177e
			</span></i>, etc.:—
				Pass.
			, of a state, <i>to be furnished with laws, have a code
				of laws,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				701d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				962e
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Hebr.</u>
				7.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>ordain by law,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				628d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				417b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐναντία τῷ ὅρκῳ τοῦ δήμου ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					4.3
				</span></i>
			: c. inf., <i>enact,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ζῴων ἐστὶν ἃ σέβεσθαι
					ἐνομοθέτησε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					11.26
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1119.16
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>: —in 
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				736c
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be ordained by law,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ep.Hebr.
				8.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ καλῶς νενομοθετημένα ἡμῖν ὑπὸ τῶν
					βασιλέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					329.13
				</span></i>
			 (Aegina, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Pr.Im.</u>
				18
			</span></i>: impers., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ ταῦτα οὕτω σφι
				νενομοθέτηται</span>
			<i>it has been</i> so <i>ordained by law,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.41
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. καλὸν [εἶναι] τὸ χαρίζεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					182b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦν νενομοθετημένον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1319a11
				</span></i>
			.</div>
